[
    {
        "content": "<p>Just putting this here to make it more visible.<br>\nFollowing our conversation with cryspen on Tuesday and the progress on hax's Lean backend, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"246591\">@Quang Dao</span> kindly compiled a minimal list of targets for extraction from Jolt's code base. This is th very first step if trying to relate some representative Rust code from a zkVM with ArkLib.<br>\n<a href=\"/user_uploads/3121/emQO00DVN1Ia3UXA7ZrxQ6i8/Minimal-extraction-surface-for-Sumcheck.pdf\">Minimal extraction surface for Sumcheck.pdf</a><br>\nFor bookeeping purposes, this is taken at commit hash  <a href=\"https://github.com/a16z/jolt/commit/2343e4b39c7fed5ec398dd4776bdac360aa76373\">2343e4b39c7fed5ec398dd4776bdac360aa76373</a> from the main branch.</p>\n<p>With several members of cryspen now also on this channel (<span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"577010\">@Karthikeyan Bhargavan</span> <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"945813\">@Maxime Buyse</span> <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"746143\">@Clément Blaudeau</span> ) we can hopefully quickly identify any issues asynchronously here. <span aria-label=\"slight smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f642\" role=\"img\" title=\"slight smile\">:slight_smile:</span></p>",
        "id": 536644330,
        "sender_full_name": "Alexander Hicks",
        "timestamp": 1756398452
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>like Alex just sent, this assumes we are in this commit (main branch today):<br>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/a16z/jolt/tree/2343e4b39c7fed5ec398dd4776bdac360aa76373\">https://github.com/a16z/jolt/tree/2343e4b39c7fed5ec398dd4776bdac360aa76373</a></p>",
        "id": 536649188,
        "sender_full_name": "Quang Dao",
        "timestamp": 1756400227
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>There are some moving around of stuff compared to a few months ago, but I think all the traits / methods remain unchanged</p>",
        "id": 536649283,
        "sender_full_name": "Quang Dao",
        "timestamp": 1756400265
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yep, good synchronisation on this and my editing it in <span aria-label=\"sweat smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f605\" role=\"img\" title=\"sweat smile\">:sweat_smile:</span></p>",
        "id": 536649302,
        "sender_full_name": "Alexander Hicks",
        "timestamp": 1756400269
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What will change in a few weeks is that challenges will only be 128 bits instead of full field elements. This is an optimization since we are overpaying for security in that part. I will let you know when that happens</p>\n<p>P/S:  we have some very cool trick to make things faster with smaller challenges (basically, interpret them as 4-limb field elements in Montgomery form, with 2 lower limbs zero. then Montgomery multiplication can skip a lot of steps, leading to 1.5x-2x faster performance)</p>",
        "id": 536649612,
        "sender_full_name": "Quang Dao",
        "timestamp": 1756400382
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This will change the API, but won't change the core protocol very much. We just interpret the challenge differently - they are still field elements, just a special subset of such</p>",
        "id": 536649894,
        "sender_full_name": "Quang Dao",
        "timestamp": 1756400465
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thank you for the document! I've started looking at the code. I'll post here if I have some questions. I'm targeting the first part \"Verifier-only\" for now</p>",
        "id": 537143707,
        "sender_full_name": "Clément Blaudeau",
        "timestamp": 1756744915
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So, I have some news regarding hax extraction! (Sorry to give them so close to the meeting, I was hoping to do it faster). I've attached the <a href=\"/user_uploads/3121/-jO0ynC7HsUpLKY7mbrNderS/Jolt_core_extracted.lean\">Lean extracted code</a> to this message. It contains the items of the \"Verifier-only\" target you sent me. We can discuss it during the meeting, or on this thread once you've had enough time to look at it.</p>\n<h2>Context</h2>\n<p>I've been working on <a href=\"https://github.com/clementblaudeau/jolt/tree/hax-lean-extract\">this fork of Jolt</a> were I've : </p>\n<ol>\n<li>Added <code>hax</code> as a dependency</li>\n<li>Added a <code>hax-extract.sh</code> script</li>\n<li>Removed default implementations in the extracted traits (we don't support those yet, so I've just copy pasted the default implementations where needed).</li>\n<li>Extracted the  <code>verify</code> function out of the impl of<code>SumcheckInstanceProof</code> to <code>extracted_SumcheckInstanceProof_impl_verify</code> just for convenience when working on it.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Then running the script just calls <code>cargo hax into lean</code> with the right set of targeted items (nothing fancy). It produces <code>proofs/lean/extraction/Jolt_Core.lean</code>. The file does not typecheck as is, so I've edited manually : </p>\n<ol>\n<li>I've added the missing bits of the <code>core</code> library as axiom at the beginning of the file </li>\n<li>Removed the impl that were extracted but out of scope of the target </li>\n<li>I've done a couple of manual edits to fix the monadic encoding (all rust computations are wrapped in a <code>Result</code> monad,  but the backend of Hax does not introduce the <code>pure</code> and <code>←</code> nodes at exactly the right spots when dealing with <code>if-then-else</code> and <code>match</code> constructs)</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The file has a remaining <code>stuck at solving universe constraint</code> error which (I believe) just comes from the axiomatisation of the lib.</p>\n<h2>Feedback</h2>\n<p>Our goal is to get the code in a shape that you can work with. So my main question is : what do you think of its shape ? Does it look usable for your needs ? (specifically, would the monadic encoding get in the way?)</p>\n<p>Beside the encoding, we can make other updates to the backend, depending on what you think is important : should names be shortened by opening namespaces locally ? Shoud the extraction produce several files instead of one ? Should typeclass constraints have predictable names ? Is the code too verbose ? <br>\netc.</p>\n<p>Finally, to have an executable code, I'll fill in the gaps in the <code>core</code> lib while waiting on your feedback.</p>",
        "id": 538662984,
        "sender_full_name": "Clément Blaudeau",
        "timestamp": 1757513574
    },
    {
        "content": "<h2>Details</h2>\n<p>Here are a few highlights of the extraction:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>All rust computations are wrapped inside a <code>Result</code> monad, which shows in the return type of functions (for instance). The <code>pure</code> operator pushes a pure computation inside the monad, while <code>←</code> lifts a monadic computation to the nearest <code>do</code> (I'm oversimplifying a bit but that's the spirit).</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">pub</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">degree</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">usize</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coeffs_except_linear_term</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">len</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Jolt_core</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Poly</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Unipoly</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Impl_9</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">degree</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[(</span><span class=\"n\">Jolt_core</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Field</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">JoltField</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">self</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Jolt_core</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Poly</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Unipoly</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CompressedUniPoly</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Result</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">usize</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Alloc</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Vec</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Impl_1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">len</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Alloc</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Alloc</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Global</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Jolt_core</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Poly</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Unipoly</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CompressedUniPoly</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coeffs_except_linear_term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">self</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Rust traits are extracted as Lean classes</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">pub</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">trait</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AppendToTranscript</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">fn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">append_to_transcript</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">ProofTranscript</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">Transcript</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">transcript</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kp\">&amp;</span><span class=\"nc\">mut</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ProofTranscript</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Jolt_core</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Transcripts</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Transcript</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AppendToTranscript</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Self</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">append_to_transcript</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ProofTranscript</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[(</span><span class=\"n\">Jolt_core</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Transcripts</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Transcript</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Transcript</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ProofTranscript</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Self</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ProofTranscript</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Result</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ProofTranscript</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Super-traits bounds are added as extra fields: </li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">pub</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">trait</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Transcript</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">Default</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">Clone</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">Sync</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">Send</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">'</span><span class=\"nb\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">fn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">new</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">label</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kp\">&amp;</span><span class=\"o\">'</span><span class=\"nb\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"kt\">u8</span><span class=\"p\">])</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">Self</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"cp\">#[cfg(test)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"o\">..</span><span class=\"p\">.</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Jolt_core</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Transcripts</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Transcript</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Transcript</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Self</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"n\">constr_8180954891579624704</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Core</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Default</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Default</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Self</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"n\">constr_15837849249852401974</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Core</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Clone</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Clone</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Self</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"n\">constr_6401136720873305866</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Core</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Marker</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Sync</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Self</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"n\">constr_252256433554570329</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Core</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Marker</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Send</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Self</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">RustSlice</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u8</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Result</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Self</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Rust structures are extracted as Lean structures (as one would expect) </li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">pub</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">struct</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">CompressedUniPoly</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">JoltField</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">pub</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">coeffs_except_linear_term</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">Vec</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Jolt_core</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Poly</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Unipoly</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CompressedUniPoly</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[(</span><span class=\"n\">Jolt_core</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Field</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">JoltField</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">coeffs_except_linear_term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Alloc</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Vec</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Vec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Alloc</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Alloc</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Global</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li>The Hax engine transforms loops into a fold operator <code>Hax.Folds.fold_range</code>. In the code of <code>eval_from_hint</code> in the impl of <code>CompressedUniPoly</code> (<code>poly/unipoly.rs</code>):</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">..</span><span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coeffs_except_linear_term</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">len</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">linear_term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coeffs_except_linear_term</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"p\">];</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Rust_primitives</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Hax</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Folds</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fold_range</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">usize</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Alloc</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Vec</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Impl_1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">len</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Alloc</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Alloc</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Global</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Jolt_core</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Poly</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Unipoly</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CompressedUniPoly</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coeffs_except_linear_term</span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"n\">self</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">linear_term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">usize</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Result</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">linear_term</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">linear_term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">usize</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Core</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Ops</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Arith</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">SubAssign</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sub_assign</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"n\">linear_term</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Core</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Ops</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Index</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Index</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">index</span>\n<span class=\"w\">              </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Jolt_core</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Poly</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Unipoly</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CompressedUniPoly</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coeffs_except_linear_term</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"n\">self</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">              </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Result</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">)))</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 538666972,
        "sender_full_name": "Clément Blaudeau",
        "timestamp": 1757514533
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(<span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"577010\">@Karthikeyan Bhargavan</span> this thread)</p>",
        "id": 538667241,
        "sender_full_name": "Clément Blaudeau",
        "timestamp": 1757514598
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I installed hax and ran the <code>./hax_extract.sh</code> script. It gave me this error:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">error</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">E0284</span><span class=\"o\">]:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">annotations</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">needed</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">note</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cannot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">satisfy</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ark_ec</span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"n\">AdditiveGroup</span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;::</span><span class=\"n\">Scalar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_`</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">error</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">E0284</span><span class=\"o\">]:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">annotations</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">needed</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">note</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cannot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">satisfy</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`&lt;&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">poly</span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"n\">commitment</span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"n\">kzg</span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"n\">Group</span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;&gt;::</span><span class=\"n\">Curve</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ark_ec</span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"n\">AdditiveGroup</span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;::</span><span class=\"n\">Scalar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_`</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This is not related to the sum-check verifier of course, but I wonder if you also encountered this when extracting. We could bump to a later commit which should fix this issue</p>",
        "id": 538693412,
        "sender_full_name": "Quang Dao",
        "timestamp": 1757521357
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'll look at it. What items were you trying to extract ? I don't recall this error specifically</p>",
        "id": 538693860,
        "sender_full_name": "Clément Blaudeau",
        "timestamp": 1757521485
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Isn't it a Rust error ? Does <code>cargo build</code> works ?</p>",
        "id": 538694022,
        "sender_full_name": "Clément Blaudeau",
        "timestamp": 1757521547
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I just ran the script. It does <code>cargo build</code> which gave that error.</p>\n<p>Also, the extracted file is standalone - where should I put it in order to get it to compile? I have cloned the hax repo.</p>",
        "id": 538694035,
        "sender_full_name": "Quang Dao",
        "timestamp": 1757521550
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You can put it in its own crate, just adding <code>hax-lib = { path = \"/path/to/your/hax/hax-lib\" }</code> in the <code>Cargo.toml</code><br>\nThen <code>cargo hax into lean</code> should work</p>",
        "id": 538694366,
        "sender_full_name": "Clément Blaudeau",
        "timestamp": 1757521648
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(also, if you want support for traits, use the <code>lean-nightly</code> branch)</p>",
        "id": 538695119,
        "sender_full_name": "Clément Blaudeau",
        "timestamp": 1757521887
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hax uses the rustc compiler for its frontend, so the code should typecheck before extraction</p>",
        "id": 538695629,
        "sender_full_name": "Clément Blaudeau",
        "timestamp": 1757522036
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Also, there is an <a href=\"https://hacspec.zulipchat.com/\">hax zulip</a> if you need help using the tool when I'm away :)</p>",
        "id": 538696003,
        "sender_full_name": "Clément Blaudeau",
        "timestamp": 1757522129
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Feels like I should wait for some more time before the workflow is more streamlined / I get a more stable version?</p>",
        "id": 538696817,
        "sender_full_name": "Quang Dao",
        "timestamp": 1757522397
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The workflow of Hax is quite well established -- the Lean ouptut is still unstable. For us, the earlier we get feedback on the shape of the output, the easier it is to make changes :) <br>\nBut the Hax engine should work on most code you throw at it (if not, it's worth opening an issue), assuming that <code>cargo check</code> passes</p>",
        "id": 538790590,
        "sender_full_name": "Clément Blaudeau",
        "timestamp": 1757576625
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"246591\">Quang Dao</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/523410-ArkLib/topic/.5Bhax.5D.20Minimal.20extraction.20surface.20for.20Sumcheck/near/538693412\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I installed hax and ran the <code>./hax_extract.sh</code> script. It gave me this error:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">error</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">E0284</span><span class=\"o\">]:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">annotations</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">needed</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">note</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cannot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">satisfy</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ark_ec</span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"n\">AdditiveGroup</span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;::</span><span class=\"n\">Scalar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_`</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">error</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">E0284</span><span class=\"o\">]:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">annotations</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">needed</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">note</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cannot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">satisfy</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`&lt;&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">poly</span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"n\">commitment</span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"n\">kzg</span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"n\">Group</span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;&gt;::</span><span class=\"n\">Curve</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ark_ec</span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"n\">AdditiveGroup</span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;::</span><span class=\"n\">Scalar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_`</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This is not related to the sum-check verifier of course, but I wonder if you also encountered this when extracting. We could bump to a later commit which should fix this issue</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I think it comes from recent changes to<code>ark_ec</code> ? I should pin it to a specific version. Although <code>cargo</code> throws this error, hax still runs and produces the extracted code right ?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Bash\"><pre><span></span><code>error<span class=\"o\">[</span>E0284<span class=\"o\">]</span>:<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>annotations<span class=\"w\"> </span>needed\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"p\">|</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>note:<span class=\"w\"> </span>cannot<span class=\"w\"> </span>satisfy<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"sb\">`</span>&lt;G<span class=\"w\"> </span>as<span class=\"w\"> </span>ark_ec::AdditiveGroup&gt;::Scalar<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>_<span class=\"sb\">`</span>\n\nerror<span class=\"o\">[</span>E0284<span class=\"o\">]</span>:<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>annotations<span class=\"w\"> </span>needed\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"p\">|</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>note:<span class=\"w\"> </span>cannot<span class=\"w\"> </span>satisfy<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"sb\">`</span><span class=\"s\">&lt;&lt;G as poly::commitment::kzg::G</span>roup&lt;P&gt;&gt;::Curve<span class=\"w\"> </span>as<span class=\"w\"> </span>ark_ec::AdditiveGroup&gt;::Scalar<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>_<span class=\"sb\">`</span>\n\nFor<span class=\"w\"> </span>more<span class=\"w\"> </span>information<span class=\"w\"> </span>about<span class=\"w\"> </span>this<span class=\"w\"> </span>error,<span class=\"w\"> </span>try<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"sb\">`</span>rustc<span class=\"w\"> </span>--explain<span class=\"w\"> </span>E0284<span class=\"sb\">`</span>.\nerror:<span class=\"w\"> </span>could<span class=\"w\"> </span>not<span class=\"w\"> </span>compile<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"sb\">`</span>jolt-core<span class=\"sb\">`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span>lib<span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>due<span class=\"w\"> </span>to<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>previous<span class=\"w\"> </span>errors\nwarning:<span class=\"w\"> </span>hax:<span class=\"w\"> </span>running<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"sb\">`</span>cargo<span class=\"w\"> </span>build<span class=\"sb\">`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>was<span class=\"w\"> </span>not<span class=\"w\"> </span>successful,<span class=\"w\"> </span>continuing<span class=\"w\"> </span>anyway.\ninfo:<span class=\"w\"> </span>hax:<span class=\"w\"> </span>wrote<span class=\"w\"> </span>file<span class=\"w\"> </span>./proofs/lean/extraction/Jolt_core.lean\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 539011815,
        "sender_full_name": "Clément Blaudeau",
        "timestamp": 1757666414
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>We use a custom version of arkworks (see top-level Cargo.toml for the patch) - I assume hax knows to get arkworks from that branch?</p>",
        "id": 539047493,
        "sender_full_name": "Quang Dao",
        "timestamp": 1757678675
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hax is plugged on rustc, so anything that cargo understand would work. In the <a href=\"https://github.com/a16z/jolt/blame/13e96f9bf3060ec47618422e423c34952b8e415b/Cargo.toml#L104\">Cargo.toml</a> there is right now :  </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"TOML\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">[patch.crates-io]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">ark-ff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">git</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"https://github.com/a16z/arkworks-algebra\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">branch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"dev/twist-shout\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"n\">ark-ec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">git</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"https://github.com/a16z/arkworks-algebra\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">branch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"dev/twist-shout\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"n\">ark-serialize</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">git</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"https://github.com/a16z/arkworks-algebra\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">branch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"dev/twist-shout\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"n\">ark-bn254</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">git</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"https://github.com/a16z/arkworks-algebra\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">branch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"dev/twist-shout\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Does <code>cargo check</code> work on your side ?</p>",
